  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Resilience Through Environmental Advocacy for Small and Other Vulnerable States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022; Amplified advocacy and representation in global climate fora: The CCFAH supports MCs in climate negotiations (e.g. UNFCCC COP30) and advocate for increased finance for climate resilience country priorities. &#x2022; Integrated policy coherence across Rio Conventions: Through the implementation of the Commonwealth Living Lands Charter, technical assistance provided to align national strategies with UNFCCC, CBD, and UNCCD goals, including the use of Indigenous knowledge and nature-based solutions. &#x2022; Gender-responsive and youth-inclusive climate action: - Operationalisation of the Commonwealth Collaborative Network on Gender-Responsive Climate Action and youth engagement platforms to ensure equitable participation in climate decision-making. - Negotiations training focused on youth engagement in global climate and environment resilience fora. &#x2022; Knowledge generation and sharing: Development of publications, workshops, and training through the Commonwealth NDC Programme and other networks to build capacity and disseminate best practices.</narrative>
  </description>
